00:10:01.665 --> 00:10:03.500
(laughter)

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.823
Nothing, nothing, you know.

00:10:04.823 --> 00:10:07.505
Really, doesn't take it personally, uh.

00:10:07.505 --> 00:10:09.142
- [Andy] What's a question
you always get asked--

00:10:09.142 --> 00:10:12.322
- You know, Dad, I'm gonna take
advantage of having you here

00:10:12.322 --> 00:10:15.585
you know, obviously we're the
same but we're very different.

00:10:15.585 --> 00:10:17.802
- But you've got a lot of me.

00:10:17.802 --> 00:10:18.638
- Yes, I know.

00:10:18.638 --> 00:10:19.880
- The better--

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.203
- The competitive thing.

00:10:21.203 --> 00:10:22.120
- Yeah.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:25.561
- But, were you interested in the fact

00:10:25.561 --> 00:10:27.024
that I'm so unphased?

00:10:27.024 --> 00:10:29.370
You, listen, there's a
lot of people watching.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.029
Tell the truth, you get upset.

00:10:31.029 --> 00:10:32.028
- Eh, about?

00:10:32.028 --> 00:10:33.363
- A lot of things.

00:10:33.363 --> 00:10:34.605
(laughter)

00:10:34.605 --> 00:10:35.708
- Uh, yes of course.

00:10:35.708 --> 00:10:36.880
I'm human, I have yeah.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.922
- But, you agree, in
business I'm kind of weird.

00:10:39.922 --> 00:10:41.884
I go into this weird state where I'm not--

00:10:41.884 --> 00:10:45.250
- He's different and he's very different.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.828
No no no, I have to hand it to him

00:10:46.828 --> 00:10:48.570
not because he's sitting here,

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.567
and I really want to give
him compliments, you know,

00:10:50.567 --> 00:10:51.821
while he's here.

00:10:51.821 --> 00:10:53.005
- Guys, just so you know, I'm fishing here

00:10:53.005 --> 00:10:55.141
because I don't get this so I'm
using advantage of the show.

00:10:55.141 --> 00:10:56.499
- But he's very different here.

00:10:56.499 --> 00:11:00.887
He made a statement, and I
can't even repeat the statement,

00:11:00.887 --> 00:11:05.079
because, to me it's against my religion--

00:11:05.079 --> 00:11:06.739
- (laughs) I don't even know.

00:11:06.739 --> 00:11:08.386
- He will do business with--

00:11:08.386 --> 00:11:09.664
- Anybody.

00:11:09.664 --> 00:11:10.941
Hitler?

00:11:10.941 --> 00:11:14.342
- You know it rubs me the wrong way,

00:11:14.342 --> 00:11:16.606
but it's true, its been proven fact.

00:11:16.606 --> 00:11:19.822
And I'm a principled guy.

00:11:19.822 --> 00:11:21.563
- I'm a principled guy!

00:11:21.563 --> 00:11:25.603
- You are, but, you put
what's good for the business

00:11:25.603 --> 00:11:26.961
before your own--

00:11:26.961 --> 00:11:27.902
- My own feelings.

00:11:27.902 --> 00:11:30.943
- Yeah, and I can't, and
I'm exactly reversed.

00:11:30.943 --> 00:11:34.581
You know, I'm, I don't know.

00:11:34.581 --> 00:11:37.233
And probably that's
what was holding me back

00:11:37.233 --> 00:11:41.632
listen, I'm not complaining,
I did pretty okay--

00:11:41.632 --> 00:11:43.026
- Yes you did, mister.

00:11:43.026 --> 00:11:45.023
- With no language, no, you know.

00:11:45.023 --> 00:11:46.323
- 100 bucks, poor.

00:11:46.323 --> 00:11:48.227
- Yeah, I can write a book and my book

00:11:48.227 --> 00:11:50.386
would be better than his,
but that's beside the point.

00:11:50.386 --> 00:11:51.384
(laughter)

00:11:51.384 --> 00:11:52.348
He's making a face.

00:11:52.348 --> 00:11:54.124
- Because it wouldn't be better.

00:11:54.124 --> 00:11:56.411
That's why I'm making a face.

00:11:56.411 --> 00:11:58.512
Let's play one on one.

00:11:58.512 --> 00:11:59.812
Show the basket.

00:11:59.812 --> 00:12:03.005
We're gonna play one
on one to settle this.

00:12:03.005 --> 00:12:05.989
- Listen, we just had my
younger son get married.

00:12:05.989 --> 00:12:07.311
- AJ, they know AJ.

00:12:07.311 --> 00:12:08.890
- Everybody knows him.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:11.769
And you would not believe what
took place at the wedding.

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:14.347
Gary gave a speech, I gave a speech.

00:12:14.347 --> 00:12:16.970
My daughter jumped in, and it became--

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:18.608
- We're a very competitive family.

00:12:18.608 --> 00:12:20.720
- Yeah, it's healthy.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.261
- Slightly unhealthy, but
I'm pumped we're unhealthy.

00:12:24.261 --> 00:12:25.886
- What do you mean unhealthy?

00:12:25.886 --> 00:12:26.989
- Well, we're very--

00:12:26.989 --> 00:12:28.022
- End of the day--

00:12:28.022 --> 00:12:29.508
- We love each other.

00:12:29.508 --> 00:12:32.956
- Even in the business, never left upset.

00:12:32.956 --> 00:12:36.137
- What, within a year?

00:12:36.137 --> 00:12:38.355
(laughter)

00:12:38.355 --> 00:12:41.350
We never left upset in a day?

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:42.917
- We kiss each other--

00:12:42.917 --> 00:12:44.670
- Well we love each other, yeah.

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:46.191
So, I don't remember the question.

00:12:46.191 --> 00:12:47.932
But I think ultimately,
Andy, there's no question

00:12:47.932 --> 00:12:49.209
that really bothers me.

00:12:49.209 --> 00:12:54.209
I think most people know the
answer to most of the questions

00:12:55.594 --> 00:12:57.161
that they ask me,

00:12:57.161 --> 00:12:58.810
I just don't think they
want to put in the work.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:01.631
And one thing that, I will say this.

00:13:01.631 --> 00:13:06.631
I think one of the best
days of my life, my life,

00:13:10.047 --> 00:13:12.926
the life that I've lived,
almost 40 years now,

00:13:12.926 --> 00:13:17.679
was when, you know it's funny,

00:13:17.679 --> 00:13:19.529
as great a day of my life,

00:13:19.529 --> 00:13:21.632
I don't fully remember
it, but I do remember

00:13:21.632 --> 00:13:24.012
several months ago, maybe within the year,

00:13:24.012 --> 00:13:27.597
maybe within 18 months,
you kind of telling me,

00:13:27.597 --> 00:13:31.048
"Man, for as hard as I
work, you work really hard."

00:13:31.048 --> 00:13:37.138
- (scoffs) Honestly, I felt at
the time, I was working hard.

00:13:37.142 --> 00:13:40.544
Sundays away, 14 hours, all this shit.

00:13:40.544 --> 00:13:45.804
This one, but thank God for his wife.

00:13:45.804 --> 00:13:48.101
I have to say this.

00:13:48.101 --> 00:13:49.947
Not every woman would--

00:13:49.947 --> 00:13:51.247
- (laughs) It's true.

00:13:51.247 --> 00:13:54.324
- He travels half a year.

00:13:54.324 --> 00:13:56.556
- These guys know.

00:13:56.556 --> 00:13:57.395
- And these guy know.

00:13:57.395 --> 00:13:59.516
- Lizzie's the best.
- Yeah--

00:13:59.516 --> 00:14:00.668
- That's why these weeks are best

00:14:00.668 --> 00:14:02.166
- I love her, I mean.

00:14:02.166 --> 00:14:04.685
As a matter of fact, I just discussed

00:14:04.685 --> 00:14:09.282
with your mom another
day about your situation.

00:14:09.282 --> 00:14:11.429
Not every woman would, you know--

00:14:11.429 --> 00:14:12.661
- Listen, it's intense.

00:14:12.661 --> 00:14:13.507
- Yeah.

00:14:13.507 --> 00:14:14.366
- We're going for it.

00:14:14.366 --> 00:14:16.120
- But you have a dream, like I had.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:19.243
When I came to this country,
I never going to forget.

00:14:19.243 --> 00:14:21.448
And listen, I don't to tell my story--

00:14:21.448 --> 00:14:23.863
- No, listen, let's do it, let's do it.

00:14:23.863 --> 00:14:27.828
- I came in 1978, and

00:14:27.828 --> 00:14:30.828
I remember I landed in JFK

00:14:30.828 --> 00:14:33.638
Pan Am, is that the name?

00:14:33.638 --> 00:14:34.439
- Pan Am.

00:14:34.439 --> 00:14:36.099
- Pan Am, there I land.

00:14:36.099 --> 00:14:38.305
- Out of business, mismanaged.

00:14:38.305 --> 00:14:42.879
- Yeah, I was walking
on Quinn's boulevard.

00:14:42.879 --> 00:14:44.759
- I know the story, go ahead.

00:14:44.759 --> 00:14:46.001
You tell them, not me.

00:14:46.001 --> 00:14:50.599
- And right there I saw a
sign, it said Alexander's.

00:14:50.599 --> 00:14:52.781
- Which was a department store,
for some of you old timers.

00:14:52.781 --> 00:14:56.986
- My actual official name was Alexander.

00:14:56.986 --> 00:14:59.956
Everybody called me Sasha, whatever.

00:14:59.956 --> 00:15:02.857
And I looked, my cousin who was already

00:15:02.857 --> 00:15:05.098
a year in this country, right?

00:15:05.098 --> 00:15:09.556
And we walked by it, and the
whole family was together,

00:15:09.556 --> 00:15:11.031
And I looked, and I said, you know,

00:15:11.031 --> 00:15:12.295
someday I'm going to have that.

00:15:12.295 --> 00:15:17.464
And she looked at me and she,
you know like, "Come on."

00:15:18.434 --> 00:15:20.510
Not exactly the same.

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:21.711
- Wine Library's very similar to that.

00:15:21.711 --> 00:15:25.530
- Yeah, so, it's, you have to have.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.255
But of course, he got bigger dream.

00:15:30.255 --> 00:15:31.648
- Well that's the way it's supposed to be.

00:15:31.648 --> 00:15:32.809
- Absolutely.

00:15:32.809 --> 00:15:37.809
To own Jets, I'm looking for
a couple of points there.

00:15:39.031 --> 00:15:40.076
- You wanna own a couple of jets there?

00:15:40.076 --> 00:15:41.272
(laughter)

00:15:41.272 --> 00:15:42.874
- Alright Andy, let's keep going.

00:15:44.702 --> 00:15:47.185
- [Voiceover] Angie asks,
"Successful leaders say

00:15:47.185 --> 00:15:49.043
"you're the sum of the five people

00:15:49.043 --> 00:15:50.622
"you spend the most time with.

00:15:50.622 --> 00:15:52.502
"How do you level up your five?"

00:15:52.502 --> 00:15:54.174
- This is an interesting question.

00:15:54.174 --> 00:15:55.764
This is something I've spent a lot of time

00:15:55.764 --> 00:15:56.937
trying to figure out.

00:15:56.937 --> 00:15:59.363
Do I, am I willing to surround myself

00:15:59.363 --> 00:16:01.221
with people who are better than me,

00:16:01.221 --> 00:16:05.238
I know it's windy, DRock,
relax, we're outside.

00:16:05.238 --> 00:16:10.978
I know, a lot of times
I've wondered if I'm

00:16:10.978 --> 00:16:13.027
surrounding myself with
people that are not.

00:16:13.027 --> 00:16:15.435
You know, I'm very nurturing.

00:16:15.435 --> 00:16:17.757
I like having a lot of people around me,

00:16:17.757 --> 00:16:19.278
I like building up people.

00:16:19.278 --> 00:16:20.322
- True.

00:16:20.322 --> 00:16:21.819
- Yeah, I like it.

00:16:21.819 --> 00:16:23.061
- Very true.

00:16:23.061 --> 00:16:25.441
Listen, not because he's my son.

00:16:25.441 --> 00:16:27.879
I don't want to sit and
brag on in front of him.

00:16:27.879 --> 00:16:31.479
He's extremely, extremely special kid.

00:16:31.479 --> 00:16:36.479
If I knew what I'm going
to get, it's a true story

00:16:37.979 --> 00:16:42.599
by the way, his mother
before we got married,

00:16:42.599 --> 00:16:46.756
said she has this thing,
she wants to have five kids.

00:16:46.756 --> 00:16:51.272
And of course, being a young
guy I say, hey, no problem.

00:16:51.272 --> 00:16:53.532
- (laughs) My parents were married at 20.

00:16:53.532 --> 00:16:55.471
- Right, we were young.

00:16:55.471 --> 00:17:00.681
And the time went on, I
got scared about education,

00:17:00.681 --> 00:17:03.574
to be able to pay, the
kids should not have loans,

00:17:03.574 --> 00:17:06.474
such nonsense, they should all have loans.

00:17:06.474 --> 00:17:08.089
- I would have paid it off easy.

00:17:08.089 --> 00:17:13.419
- Right, and so, he's,
again I'm not going to

00:17:13.419 --> 00:17:14.951
sit and brag about you--

00:17:14.951 --> 00:17:17.376
- I think I might have you
on the show more often.

00:17:17.376 --> 00:17:19.127
This is, I'm feeling nice.

00:17:19.127 --> 00:17:23.807
- I'm being very honest with you,

00:17:23.807 --> 00:17:25.887
maybe somebody out there

00:17:25.887 --> 00:17:27.951
who's going to stumble
on this video, whatever.

00:17:27.951 --> 00:17:31.665
His DNA should be bottled.

00:17:31.665 --> 00:17:35.345
I'm very serious, not
because we had four wines.

00:17:35.345 --> 00:17:40.475
Well, that helps, but,
I mean, he's extremely,

00:17:40.475 --> 00:17:44.807
extremely special in many ways.

00:17:48.747 --> 00:17:52.195
And Barack Obama doesn't
invite him to the White House.

00:17:52.195 --> 00:17:56.676
- Please, this is nice enough,
you don't have to get crazy.

00:17:56.676 --> 00:17:59.036
- Just because,

00:17:59.036 --> 00:18:03.435
as a father I'm very proud.

00:18:03.435 --> 00:18:06.419
In the business, we had
a lot of disagreements.

00:18:06.419 --> 00:18:07.301
(laughter)

00:18:07.301 --> 00:18:10.842
- We could disagree about the
color of the goddamn thing.

00:18:10.842 --> 00:18:15.842
But end of the day, we
bounce off each other things.

00:18:17.018 --> 00:18:21.174
And I don't think Gary
ever mentions that because

00:18:21.174 --> 00:18:23.275
he's a very competitive guy.

00:18:23.275 --> 00:18:26.305
But a lot of good ideas,
and I don't want to put

00:18:26.305 --> 00:18:29.521
myself somewhere, but a
lot of them beginning,

00:18:29.521 --> 00:18:34.521
was Wine Library, it came
driving an hour each way

00:18:34.523 --> 00:18:35.918
- I wrote a Medium--

00:18:35.918 --> 00:18:38.784
- I miss it so much.

00:18:38.784 --> 00:18:40.386
I miss it so much.

00:18:40.386 --> 00:18:44.055
And I understand, listen,
he's got things going on,

00:18:44.055 --> 00:18:48.779
but that part I always miss because

00:18:48.779 --> 00:18:50.719
it was very special.

00:18:50.719 --> 00:18:55.316
You know even today when
the family get together,

00:18:58.402 --> 00:19:02.173
it's, even my daughter's
birthday was a couple days ago,

00:19:02.173 --> 00:19:04.590
you know she turned what, 30?

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:05.763
- Six.

00:19:05.763 --> 00:19:06.889
- Right.

00:19:06.889 --> 00:19:07.864
- Sorry Liz.

00:19:07.864 --> 00:19:12.611
- Yeah, no but even her
friends saw the dynamic

00:19:12.611 --> 00:19:15.886
of our family, and I
have to give it to mom.

00:19:15.886 --> 00:19:19.229
Mom built a very strong foundation.

00:19:19.229 --> 00:19:23.408
Who grew up without a mother, you know.

00:19:23.408 --> 00:19:26.485
She was at age five, she lost her mother,

00:19:26.485 --> 00:19:31.955
and but she's very special person

00:19:31.955 --> 00:19:36.770
who built this family, and you know,

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:39.545
I work and she was building the family.

00:19:39.545 --> 00:19:43.591
It's a great combination,
and it's you know

00:19:43.591 --> 00:19:48.101
I'm very proud what this
family were able to accomplish,

00:19:48.108 --> 00:19:51.346
and especially what Gary and AJ.

00:19:51.346 --> 00:19:55.189
I mean you know, special kids definitely.

00:19:55.189 --> 00:19:58.904
All of them, and I see grandchildren,

00:19:58.904 --> 00:20:01.783
Oliver and you know.

00:20:01.783 --> 00:20:03.942
- Alexander.

00:20:03.942 --> 00:20:05.370
- Alexander.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:07.123
- Alexander is eating a lot of olives,

00:20:07.123 --> 00:20:08.725
so we decided to name him Olive.

00:20:08.725 --> 00:20:11.569
- He wants to call himself Olive.

00:20:11.569 --> 00:20:16.569
And that's a really real
special, real special.

00:20:16.863 --> 00:20:20.310
- Thanks dad, I have no idea
Andy what the question was.

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:21.444
But, what was it again?

00:20:21.444 --> 00:20:22.378
- [Voiceover] Sum of the five

00:20:22.378 --> 00:20:23.610
people you spend the most time with?

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:27.092
- Yeah I mean, I think
that, yeah I think I have.

00:20:27.092 --> 00:20:29.730
I definitely over the
last five to seven years

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:33.755
surround myself with
higher caliber characters.

00:20:33.755 --> 00:20:35.731
I think it's a commitment, I think,

00:20:35.731 --> 00:20:38.690
but on the flip-side, I'm
very comfortable in bringing

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:41.987
value to the people
that maybe aren't better

00:20:41.987 --> 00:20:45.249
than me, I think giving
back is massively important.

00:20:45.249 --> 00:20:48.696
I think it's, there's a level of karma,

00:20:48.696 --> 00:20:52.365
and I think as long as you're focused on

00:20:52.365 --> 00:20:53.689
surrounding yourself with five people

00:20:53.689 --> 00:20:56.834
that can bring your level up,
I think the real answer is

00:20:56.834 --> 00:20:58.913
it's about 10, right, I think it's about

00:20:58.913 --> 00:21:01.768
creating a scenario where
you have five people

00:21:01.768 --> 00:21:03.904
that are leveling you up,
and I think it's about

00:21:03.904 --> 00:21:06.389
surrounding yourself with five people

00:21:06.389 --> 00:21:08.914
that you level up, and I think

00:21:08.914 --> 00:21:11.926
I think I get tremendous enjoyment on

00:21:11.926 --> 00:21:14.537
leveling up the five people around me.

00:21:14.537 --> 00:21:17.433
- [Voiceover] Chris asks,
"I got a question for ya.

00:21:17.433 --> 00:21:21.628
"How bad do you wish Tom
Brady was your quarterback?"

00:21:21.628 --> 00:21:23.044
- What is this again?

00:21:23.044 --> 00:21:24.529
- The question is how bad do I want

00:21:24.529 --> 00:21:26.863
Tom Brady to be my quarterback?

00:21:30.073 --> 00:21:31.472
- You don't.

00:21:31.472 --> 00:21:34.536
- I'll take him, I mean look.

00:21:34.536 --> 00:21:37.276
Brett Favre was probably
one of the five players

00:21:37.276 --> 00:21:38.855
I disliked the most in the NFL,

00:21:38.855 --> 00:21:40.515
but I've said it before on the show,

00:21:40.515 --> 00:21:43.394
the second that a player takes on my logo,

00:21:43.394 --> 00:21:45.391
they're alright, right?

00:21:45.391 --> 00:21:46.332
- That's true.

00:21:46.332 --> 00:21:47.945
- Wayne Gretzky we didn't like, I liked,

00:21:47.945 --> 00:21:49.815
well my dad's a Devils
fan, I'm a Rangers fan,

00:21:49.815 --> 00:21:53.947
but I think, you know
he's getting a little old.

00:21:53.947 --> 00:21:57.952
I think he's, listen, I would cut my,

00:21:57.952 --> 00:22:00.947
I'm going to say this,
I would cut my entire

00:22:00.947 --> 00:22:04.266
right arm off, I would, sit calm,

00:22:04.266 --> 00:22:09.257
I would cut my entire right,

00:22:09.257 --> 00:22:12.747
left arm off for Aaron Rodgers

00:22:12.747 --> 00:22:14.573
because I think we would
win the Super Bowl.

00:22:14.573 --> 00:22:16.072
I think Aaron Rodgers is the best quarter

00:22:16.072 --> 00:22:18.428
well Andrew Luck, I would
cut my entire left arm off

00:22:18.428 --> 00:22:21.028
for Andrew Luck, I'm going Indianapolis

00:22:21.028 --> 00:22:22.526
for week two.

